      "type": "local",
      "reason": "The displayed contraction \u03b4^c_b g^{ab} equals g^{ab}, not \u03b4^a_b; remove this false duplicate or replace it with the correct inverse-matrix identity."
    },
    {
      "id": "def-gr-si-unit-and-coordinate-conventions",
      "type": "scope",
      "reason": "The item assigns units to \u03c4, U, R, Ric and S before defining them; their suppliers def-gr-timelike-worldline-and-proper-time (GR02) and def-gr-curvature-tensor-and-derived-tensors (GR04) are later, \u0393 lacks def-christoffel-symbols-of-an-affine-connection, and def-gr-stress-energy-tensor-field uses the forward T convention."
    },
    {
      "id": "lem-gr-connection-conditions-in-chart-components",
      "type": "local",
      "reason": "The formula, facts and proof use indices and sums 1..4 although the GR four-dimensional convention is 0..3; align them with the declared index system."
    },
    {
      "id": "def-gr-stress-energy-tensor-field",
      "type": "scope",
      "reason": "All orthonormal T_AB components are assigned J/m\u00b3, yet off-diagonal entries are described as energy flux and momentum density without c conversions or requiring future-directed e_0; define the observer readings and SI factors."
    },
    {
      "id": "post-gr-spacetime-and-classical-domain",
      "type": "scope",
      "reason": "The postulate says g's curvature represents gravity without identifying the connection or defining curvature; the later GR03/04 suppliers thm-gr-nondegenerate-levi-civita-and-tensor-derivative and def-gr-curvature-tensor-and-derived-tensors leave an unresolved definition-order obligation."
    },
    {
      "id": "ex-gr-spherical-coordinates-flat-metric-components",
      "type": "local",
      "reason": "The cited inverse-function theorem proves only a local diffeomorphism; step 2.1 also needs the global open-image and smooth-inverse consequence for the injective map, which should be derived by openness and gluing the local inverses."
    },
    {
      "id": "def-gr-energy-conditions",
      "type": "local",
      "reason": "The remark says WEC, NEC and DEC are unordered, but the stated definitions give WEC \u21d2 NEC by a timelike limit and DEC \u21d2 WEC; replace the false assertion with the actual implication scope."
    },
    {
      "id": "def-gr-measured-energy-density-flux-and-stress",
